From e6bff25137ab9e3867af67fc3d0c1384806e7a1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:18:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(providers): a pooled-credential provider and a
 provider-owned fallback route

Two seams in the provider profile, used by the Claude plugin for the pooled API credit provider (claude-credits) and the account pool (claude-pool).

anthropic_transport(session_id, timeout): a provider whose API key is chosen per request returns the httpx transport its Anthropic client sends through. The provider's key is the placeholder "hermes-pooled-key/<profile name>"; build_anthropic_client builds the SDK client over the profile's transport when it sees that key, so the agent, a fallback swap, the primary restore, a model switch and auxiliary calls all pool the same way and no real key sits in a client. The chat's session id rides on the key ("#<session>") so the transport keeps its books per chat.

fallback_route(model) and primary_ready(model): a provider names where its calls go when it has nothing left to try (the pool: the same model on the pooled API credits), and says when it can serve again. The route goes first in the agent's fallback chain while the agent runs on the provider; an error that carries hermes_user_message (0099, a pool with no account left) tries it before ending the turn with the line. The agent goes back to the provider before the next model call as soon as primary_ready says so, whatever cooldown the fallback armed, and a new turn does the same. A provider that overrides none of the hooks changes nothing. Subagents, scheduled jobs and chats run the same loop.
